---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-confirm-dialog</code> asks one question before an action runs, so apps don't build
  their own "Are you sure?" modal. Put the question in <code>headline</code> and the message in the
  default slot: say what will happen and whether it can be undone. Name the action on the confirm
  button with <code>confirm-label</code>; the defaults are "Confirm" and "Cancel".
</p>
<p>
  It opens in the top layer like <code>wc-modal</code>, with the <code>alertdialog</code> role: the
  headline is its accessible name and the message its description. Confirm gets the initial focus.
  Escape and Cancel close it; a click on the scrim does not, because a confirmation needs an
  explicit answer.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-button id='confirm-dialog-simple-open'>Discard changes</wc-button>
  <wc-confirm-dialog
    id='confirm-dialog-simple'
    headline='Discard changes?'
    confirm-label='Discard'
  >
    Your edits to this page are not saved and will be lost.
  </wc-confirm-dialog>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      const dialog = document.querySelector('#confirm-dialog-simple');
      document
        .querySelector('#confirm-dialog-simple-open')
        .addEventListener('click', () => dialog.show());
      dialog.addEventListener('close', event => {
        myConsole.log(`close: ${JSON.stringify(event.detail)}`);
      });
    })();
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Events</h3>
<p>
  <code>confirm</code> fires when the person confirms. <code>close</code> fires whenever the dialog
  closes, with <code>detail.reason</code> (<code>'action'</code> for either button,
  <code>'escape'</code>, or <code>'api'</code> for <code>hide()</code>) and
  <code>detail.confirmed</code>, which says whether the person confirmed. Use
  <code>confirmed</code> rather than the reason to tell the two buttons apart.
</p>
